---
// Teen IOP, "Why in-person matters for teens". Sage: an illustrated scene, a phone screen giving way to a circle.
// Simplified 2026-11-18 (user: graphics too busy): few big elements, large icon circles, little text, in the style
// of conditions/OcdGraphic.astro and the DBT wheel. Facts are in the bullets beside it. Styles: programs.css (.gx-*).
---
<figure class="gx t-sage" aria-label="From behind a screen to face to face: a room with peers who get it and clinicians who know their name">
  <svg class="gx-svg ip" viewBox="0 0 330 182" aria-hidden="true">
    <rect x="24" y="24" width="64" height="108" rx="12" class="ph" /><rect x="32" y="36" width="48" height="76" rx="4" class="scr" /><circle cx="56" cy="121" r="4" class="scr" />
    <path d="M108 78 H146" class="ar" /><path d="M138 70 L147 78 L138 86" class="ar" />
    <circle cx="240" cy="78" r="34" class="tb" />
    {[0, 60, 120, 180, 240, 300].map((a) => <circle cx={240 + 56 * Math.cos((a - 90) * Math.PI / 180)} cy={78 + 56 * Math.sin((a - 90) * Math.PI / 180)} r="13" class:list={["p", a === 0 && "g"]} />)}
    <text x="56" y="175" class="l1">Behind a screen</text><text x="240" y="175" class="l2">Face to face</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="gx-cap">Peers who get it, clinicians who know their name</figcaption>
</figure>
